course: dictionary
lesson: 12449
title: Deduction: taking away or working it out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deduction has three meanings. It can be an amount taken away from a total, like a deduction from your pay. It can be working something out by reasoning from facts you know, the way a detective does. It can also be the conclusion you reach that way.
explain: «The tax deduction came off his wages before he was paid.» Here the word means money taken away from a total. Ask yourself: is something being subtracted? If yes, it is the first meaning.
explain: «Her powers of deduction helped her solve the case.» Here the word means working out the answer from clues. Clue words like solve and clues tell you this is the second meaning.
explain: «By deduction, Sam knew the cake was gone, because he was the only one in the kitchen.» Here the deduction is the conclusion Sam reached. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Deduction is a noun. Its plural is deductions.
fact: «Deduction» means an amount taken away from a total, or working something out by reasoning from facts.
fact: «Deduction» can also mean the conclusion you reach by reasoning.
fact: Useful phrases: a tax deduction, powers of deduction, by deduction.
fact: In maths, deductions of money or points mean subtraction.
exercise: «The shop gave a deduction of two pounds from the price.» What does deduction mean here? | A detective's clever guess | *An amount taken away from a total | A reason why the shop is open | A sale that makes the price bigger
exercise: «The detective used careful deduction to find the thief.» What does deduction mean here? | A total of all the points | A loud noise in the hall | A payment for a new coat | *Working out the answer from facts and clues
exercise: Mia says, «The lights are on and the car is here, so Dad must be home. That is my deduction.» What is a deduction here? | A total of all the points | A loud noise in the hall | A tax taken off her pay | *A conclusion reached by reasoning from facts
test: Ravi had 20 points, and 5 points were a deduction for talking. How many points does he have left? | 5 | 20 | 25 | *15
test: Which phrase means finding the answer by reasoning from clues? | Tax deduction | Points total | *By deduction | Half price
exam: «Her powers of deduction helped her spot the lie.» What does deduction mean here? | Money taken off a bill | A loud argument | *Clever reasoning from facts to reach a conclusion | A sale price
